# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets redirects/rewrites file (same format as
# Cloudflare Pages: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/).
#
# The profile-exchange share link (`https://2026.flutterkaigi.jp/x/<token>`,
# see apps/app/lib/feature/exchange/data/exchange_link.dart) is opened by a
# browser only when the app isn't installed / Universal Links / App Links
# didn't intercept it. jaspr's static-site generation can't pre-render one
# page per possible token, so every `/x/<token>` request is rewritten
# (200 = rewrite, keeps the URL bar as-is) to the single generated fallback
# page instead — see lib/pages/app_link_fallback.dart. The token itself is
# never read or forwarded anywhere; this is a static asset lookup at the
# Cloudflare edge, not a server request carrying the token onward.
#
# The rewrite destination is `/x`, NOT `/x/index.html` or `/x/` — Cloudflare
# rejects this file at deploy time ("Invalid _redirects configuration ...
# Infinite loop detected", code 100324) for either of those. Its validator
# applies the platform's default `html_handling` normalization (which strips
# a trailing `/index.html`, `/index`, or `.html` from a path) to the rewrite
# destination and re-checks it against every rule's source pattern; both
# `/x/index.html` and `/x/` normalize to `/x/`, which still matches this
# rule's own source glob `/x/*` (a glob's trailing `/*` matches a path ending
# in just `/`, since `*` matches the empty string) — so the platform judges
# the rule as pointing back into itself. `/x` (no trailing slash, no `.html`
# suffix) has nothing left to strip, and doesn't start with `/x/`, so it
# cannot re-match `/x/*`: no loop, by the same rule the validator applies.
# Static asset resolution for a 200 rewrite still finds the generated
# `x/index.html` at that destination through ordinary directory-index
# lookup, without re-running redirect/normalization logic against it (that
# logic only fires for the *original*, user-facing request) — confirmed by
# inspecting the jaspr build output (`build/jaspr/x/index.html`), which is
# unaffected by this change; only this rewrite target moved.
/x/*    /x    200
